        "original_id": "fb3f08b3-4677-5633-9b31-7c050e9fc8c1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Frailea, Cyathodes, Frailea castanea, Gymnocalycium eurypleurum\n- Concepts: cactus genera, shrub genera, species distribution, plant association\n\nFacts:\n- Frailea is a genus of globular to short cylindrical cacti native to Brazil.\n- Cyathodes is a genus of shrubs in the heath family.\n- Frailea castanea is a species in the genus Frailea found in Argentina, Brazil, and Uruguay.\n- Gymnocalycium eurypleurum is almost always solitary in the wild and may grow in association with Frailea species.",
